{{Quote|Do I look ''stupid'' to you? Am I a Gamorrean?|A [[Krawg]] [[pirate]]|<ref name="Star Wars (2015) 34">[[Star Wars (2015) 34|''Star Wars'' (2015) 34]]</ref>}}
'''Gamorreans''', derogatorily known as "'''pigs'''," were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] of [[Color|green]]-skinned [[pig]]-like [[humanoid]]s that [[Homeworld|hailed]] from the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]] of [[Gamorr]]. They grouped themselves in clans, each of which was led by a [[Warlord (Gamorrean)|warlord]] and a [[Clan Matron]]. A number of Gamorreans were employed by the [[crime lord]] [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba]] the [[Hutt]] to act as guards throughout his career.

==Biology and appearance==
[[File:GamorreanGuard-CGSWG.png|thumb|200px|left|Gamorreans had porcine features.]]
A [[species]] of tall, strong [[Humanoid|bipeds]], the Gamorreans had [[porcine]] traits,<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" /> like an upturned, large-nostriled cartilaginous [[Nose|snout]],<ref name="RotJ paperback novel">[[Star Wars: Return of the Jedi (paperback novel)|''Star Wars: Return of the Jedi'' junior novelization]]</ref> jowls, and upturned tusks.<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" /> Gamorrean younglings had baby teeth that would irritate them and eventually come loose after some time.<ref name="Gamorrean GP">{{GalacticPals|Gamorrean}}</ref> Their hulking bodies were covered in [[Color|green]]<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" /> or rarely pink,<ref name="Droid Hunters" /> thick and [[hair]]less skin. They had five digits on every extremity, each sporting a hard nail. The digits of their hands included an opposable thumb, which allowed the Gamorreans to easily grasp and handle objects. The species had two [[Gender|sexes]]: the males, referred to as boars, and the females, called sows.<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" /> Other species used the term "pig" to insult Gamorreans.<ref name="Midnight Horizon">''[[The High Republic: Midnight Horizon]]''</ref>

==Society and culture==
Gamorreans had a clan-based society. Each clan was ruled by a female leader, the [[Clan Matron]], and a male leader, the [[Warlord (Gamorrean)|Warlord]].<ref name="Warlord">''[[Star Wars: Uprising]]''&mdash;Crew Member: "Gamorrean Warlord"</ref> Although the sows [[farm]]ed and [[Hunting|hunted]] while the boars waged wars,<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" /> the Gamorrean society was in fact a matriarchy. Indeed, a Warlord held his position by way of [[marriage]] to a Matron rather than force, although Matrons did make their selections based on the boars' combat skills.<ref name="Warlord" /> Gamorreans saw war as glorious, and violent clashes between clans were rife.<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" />

[[File:PatrollingtheWastes-TitF.png|thumb|right|250px|A group of Jabba's Gamorrean guards partrol the desert in a skiff.]]
Because of their low intelligence, Gamorreans tended to be both stubborn and loyal; philosophically, they believed that any problem could be solved by hitting it with brute force. They had a [[language]] of their own that sounded like mere grunts and squeals to outsiders. Although they could understand other languages, such as [[Galactic Basic Standard]], they found most of them too difficult to pronounce.<ref name="Aliens of the Galaxy" /> Gamorreans respected those who used swears in the Gamorrean language, loving to use insults against others and their families. Their love of vulgarity meant they were not always annoyed when they were referred to as "pigs."<ref name="Midnight Horizon" />

Technologically speaking, the Gamorreans were primitive, and they favored [[melee weapon]]s like [[vibro-ax]]es,<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" /> such as the [[Arg'garok]],<ref name="SWC">''[[Star Wars: Commander]]''</ref> [[vibro-lance]]s,<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" /> and [[Gamorrean war ax|Gamorrean battle-axes]]<ref name="Target Vader 4">[[Target Vader 4|''Target Vader'' 4]]</ref> over [[blaster]]s.<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" /> They never discovered space travel on their own. Moreover, Gamorrean boars failed to maintain personal hygiene, rarely changing their clothes or wiping the streaming mucus from under their snouts.<ref name="beware">''[[Return of the Jedi: Beware the Power of the Dark Side!]]''</ref> Gamorreans chopped down areas of their natural [[forest]] habitat to make room for [[farm]]ing.<ref name="VE" />

==History==
Gamorreans evolved on the [[planet]] of [[Gamorr]] in the [[Outer Rim Territories]].<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" />

==Gamorreans in the galaxy==
===Criminal agents and other passions===
{{Quote|Drop your weapons or ''die'', Tusken ''trash!'|translated=1|A Gammorean guard of Jabba the Hutt's palace|<ref name="Age of Rebellion - Jabba the Hutt 1">[[Age of Rebellion - Jabba the Hutt 1|''Age of Rebellion - Jabba the Hutt'' 1]]</ref>}}
[[File:Gamorrean_prisoner_SaV.png|thumb|left|220px|A [[tattoo]]ed and [[Piercing|pierced]] Gamorrean [[prisoner]]]]
Offworld Gamorreans were a common sight, be they [[Mercenary|mercenaries]] or enforcers working for [[crime lord]]s.<ref name="Aliens of the Galaxy" /> Such enforcers were mercenaries known as [[Gamorrean Warrior]]s,<ref name="SWC" /> otherwise known as Gamorrean Guards.<ref name="Topps">{{ToppsLivingSet|num=38|cardname=Gamorrean Guard|link=https://www.tcdb.com/ViewCard.cfm/sid/205515/cid/13683410/2019-Topps-Living-Star-Wars-38-Gamorrean-Guard}}</ref> Most notably, the [[Hutt]] gangster [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]] employed Gamorrean guards throughout his career.<ref name="Aliens of the Galaxy" /> The overall [[Hutt Clan]], of which [[Jabba's criminal empire]] was part, made use of Gamorrean Guards, including on its capital world of [[Nal Hutta]].<ref name="Hunt for Ziro">{{TCW|Hunt for Ziro}}</ref> The Hutt crime lord [[Bokku]] also employed Gamorreans.<ref name="Vader 12">[[Darth Vader (2020) 12|''Darth Vader'' (2020) 12]]</ref> 

As mercenaries, Gamorrean Warriors were open to work with numerous factions, including the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] and [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="SWC" /> Upon being hired, however, Gamorreans could display a great loyalty to their client.<ref name="Boba Chap 1">{{BOBF|Chapter 1: Stranger in a Strange Land}}</ref> Uncharacteristically, a Gamorrean worked as a [[clown]] in [[Preigo]]'s [[Preigo's Traveling World of Wonder|Traveling World of Wonder]] at the time of the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="Bound">{{TCW|Bound for Rescue}}</ref> In underground [[gladiator]] matches, Gamorreans often served as powerhouse fighters.<ref name="DB Fighters">{{Databank|gamorrean-fighters|Gamorrean fighters}}</ref> In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="9 ABY date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' establishes that ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'' is set in [[9 ABY]].</ref> two Gamorreans dueled with vibro-axes for sport in an arena in<ref name="Chapter 9">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 9: The Marshal}}</ref> one such underground match.<ref name="DB Fighters" /> A Gamorrean named [[Gork]] worked for the gang of [[pirate]]s [[Kragan Gorr]]'s [[Warbird gang]].<ref name="No Escape Part 2">{{Resistance|No Escape: Part 2}}</ref>

Of Jabba the Hutt's Gamorrean Guards, [[Unidentified Gamorrean guard 1|two]] [[Unidentified Gamorrean guard 2|guards]] managed to survive past both Jabba's [[Rescue of Han Solo|demise]] and [[Attack on Jabba's Palace (Boba Fett)|that of his successor]], [[Bib Fortuna]]. The two guards displayed great loyalty to both of their bosses. Both guards were brought before Fortuna's usurper, the former [[bounty hunter]] and self-declared [[Daimyo]] [[Boba Fett]], who offered both employment in return for the same loyalty they had shown his forebears. Both Gamorreans quickly kneeled before Fett<ref name="Boba Chap 1" /> and aided him in his efforts to cement control over the planet [[Tatooine]], ending with their deaths at the [[Battle of Mos Espa]].<ref name="Boba Chap 7">{{BOBF|Chapter 7: In the Name of Honor}}</ref>

===Creations of Restin===
[[File:GamorreanCranwell-ShadowOfVadersCastle.jpg|thumb|right|220px|Cranwell, according to a story told by Vaneé, became an artificial Gamorrean.]]
According to a tale told by [[Acolytes of the Beyond|Acolyte of the Beyond]] [[Vaneé]], at some point after the [[Destruction of Alderaan|destruction]] of the planet [[Alderaan]], [[Doctor]] [[Restin]] of the [[Tarkin Initiative]] vowed to have revenge on the [[Sith Lord]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] for the deaths of his family and friends. Working with his [[droid]]s, he created a [[Gamorrean Serum|genetic serum]] that, after injection, would turn its subject into a Gamorrean after hearing a certain soundwave; a Gamorrean squeal. This infection could then spread by touch. Upon learning of this, the scientist's assistant, [[Cranwell]], contacted Vader's [[Star Destroyer]] to warn him of Restin's betrayal and then tried to stop the doctor's work, though this only resulted in his capture. When Vader arrived, feigning ignorance of the doctor's true intentions and, after witnessing Restin turn Cranwell into a Gamorrean, suggesting they could use the infection against the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]], Restin released his unstable Gamorrean against the [[Sith]] [[Lord]].<ref name="Shadow of Vader's Castle">''[[Star Wars Adventures: Shadow of Vader's Castle]]''</ref>

The former assistant transformed Vader's [[stormtrooper]]s into Gamorreans, but the [[Dark Lord of the Sith]] effortlessly [[Telekinesis|lifted]] the infected and Restin into the air with [[the Force]]. After forcing the scientist to confess, Vader revealed that he had only come to be a first-hand witness to his defeat, as the Sith Lord then used the Force to push the Gamorreans into the doctor, making them infect their very creator. Vader then departed aboard his [[Lambda-class T-4a shuttle|''Lambda''-class T-4a shuttle]], leaving the infected Restin at the mercy of his creations. When he told the story, Vaneé explained Vader had not been afraid of turning into a Gamorrean because, as he put it, Vader already was a monster.<ref name="Shadow of Vader's Castle" />

